WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.802
When a cleaning rule is strong enough to update data, use a controlled workflow.

00:00:04.802 --> 00:00:08.337
Preview with SELECT. Start a transaction.

00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:10.877
Run UPDATE with a narrow condition.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:14.022
Use RETURNING to inspect the changed rows.

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:17.782
Then either commit the change or roll it back.

00:00:17.782 --> 00:00:21.052
This makes destructive cleaning much safer.

00:00:21.052 --> 00:00:26.542
Once a quality rule is well understood, prevention may be better than repeated cleanup.

00:00:26.542 --> 00:00:30.552
Constraints can stop known invalid values at write time.

00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:34.227
When updates are required, preview the target rows, change only what is justified,

00:00:34.227 --> 00:00:40.080
and use RETURNING or an audit log so the transformation can be reviewed.
